# MetaTwo

**Platform:** HackTheBox
**OS:** Linux
**Tags:** BookingPress, CVE-2022-0739, SQLi, WordPress, CVE-2021-29447, XXE, FTP, Passpie, PGP
**Date:** 2026-10-22

A WordPress site running BookingPress 1.0.10, vulnerable to unauthenticated SQL injection via CVE-2022-0739. The extracted hash cracks to a valid WordPress login. WordPress 5.6.2 on PHP 8 resolves external entities in uploaded WAV file metadata, leaking arbitrary files including wp-config.php with FTP credentials. FTP exposes a mailer directory containing SMTP credentials for jnelson, who reuses them as SSH password. Root comes from a Passpie vault whose PGP master key cracks in seconds.

## 1. Enumeration

```bash
nmap -sC -sV <TARGET_IP>
nmap -sC -sV -p- <TARGET_IP>
```

```
21/tcp  open  ftp     vsftpd
22/tcp  open  ssh     OpenSSH 8.4p1 Debian
80/tcp  open  http    nginx 1.18.0
```

Port 80 redirects to `metapress.htb`. Added it to `/etc/hosts`. FTP on 21 and SSH on 22 are also open.

VHost fuzzing with ffuf found nothing additional. Gobuster on the web root turned up `/wp-admin`, `/wp-login.php`, and `/events`.

```bash
ffuf -w /usr/share/seclists/Discovery/DNS/subdomains-top1million-5000.txt -u http://metapress.htb/ -H "Host: FUZZ.metapress.htb" -fs <size>
gobuster dir -u http://metapress.htb/ -w /usr/share/seclists/Discovery/Web-Content/raft-medium-directories.txt
```

